event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"command\": \"mkdir -p ~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output\\ncat \u003e ~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/final-report.md \u003c\u003c'EOF'\\n# Campaign csrclaude — final report\\n\\n## Mission\\nDeliver `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string, with\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\\n\\n## Outcome: met\\n\\n## What happened\\n- d001 (briefing confirmation) exchanged with dev; accepted.\\n- d002 dispatched to dev with the full spec (both deliverables, the exact\\n  verification command, and a requirement to self-verify before replying).\\n- dev replied with: `src/greet.py` (`return \\\"Hello, {}!\\\".format(name)`),\\n  `tests/test_greet.py` (test_normal_name asserting `greet(\\\"Alice\\\") ==\\n  \\\"Hello, Alice!\\\"`, test_empty_name asserting `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`),\\n  committed as `22127ab` on `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`\\n  (parent = base `1053761f`), and a reported clean `unittest discover` run\\n  (2 tests, OK, exit 0).\\n- Verified independently rather than trusting the report: fetched\\n  `refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`, read the actual diff (only the two\\n  expected files touched, no scope creep), checked out the commit into an\\n  isolated worktree, and re-ran `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n  myself — 2 tests, OK, exit 0.\\n- Accepted dev's d002 reply on the first attempt; no rework was required.\\n\\n## Criteria check\\n1. `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` → `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` — met.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string — met.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 — met (confirmed\\n   independently, not just via dev's report).\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied. Nothing is unmet.\\nEOF\\ncat ~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/final-report.md\", \"description\": \"Write durable final report to campaign output directory\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

